course: dictionary
lesson: 13720
title: Following instructions
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Instructions are words that tell you how to do something, step by step. «Read the instructions before you start the model.» The instructions tell you the order to work in, so you do not have to guess what comes next.
explain: Instructions can also be orders from someone in charge. «The teacher gave clear instructions for the test.» Here the word means what the teacher wants you to do, not a list of steps for making something.
explain: Instructions are usually written as bossy verbs, like «cut», «mix» and «place». In computing, instructions are commands that tell a computer exactly what to do, in the right order.
fact: Instructions is a noun, and it is usually used in the plural.
fact: «Instructions» means words that tell you how to do something, step by step.
fact: «Instructions» can also mean orders that tell someone what to do.
fact: In computing, instructions are commands that tell a computer what to do.
fact: One single step or order is called an instruction.
exercise: «Follow the instructions to build the model.» What are instructions? | A kind of puzzle with no answer | *Words that tell you how to do something, step by step | A picture of a model | A word for a finished model
exercise: «The teacher gave clear instructions for the test.» What does instructions mean here? | Questions the teacher can't answer | Things that are broken | *Orders telling you what to do | A list of your favourite foods
exercise: Maya reads the instructions before she mixes the cake. Why does this help her? | She can skip the steps she doesn't like | *She knows the steps and their order | She can make the cake without any ingredients | She gets to eat the cake sooner
test:
Find the word that means one single order or step. | instruction | instructions | instructing | instructed
Which is an example of step-by-step instructions? | *First cut the apple, then mix it with the yoghurt | The apple is red and sweet | Apples grow on trees in orchards | I like apples more than pears
exam:
«In computing, instructions must be exact and in the right order.» Why? | *Because the computer does exactly what each command says, in the order given | Because computers enjoy solving puzzles and like neat lists | Because the computer will ignore any command that is not in capitals | Because instructions are always optional for computers
